<urn:atm:triage:finding/CPR-010>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "CPR-010" ;
  triage:title "Design section 5.2's ORDERING RULE is violated for close rejections: the completion report is destroyed" ;
  triage:description "Hostile closure review (general-purpose opus, task af4edaf6699568f49) @ 9f5aef2fe. Design §5.2's ORDERING RULE is violated for close rejections: the completion report is destroyed. Doc says: nudge-task-design.md §5.2: 'ORDERING RULE: deliver the message first, then apply the close. A close that fails must never destroy the report.' Code does: Message insert and close run in one savepoint (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/ops.rs:704-735 — `apply_task_message(record, ...)?` aborts the whole op). On rejection, batch.rs drops the savepoint, rolling back the mail row. Two rejection modes hit this: third-party close (crates/atm-storage/src/task_state.rs:297-304) and stale counterparty (task_ops.rs:564-569). Recommendation: Give the authorization and staleness rejections a deliver-plain fallback like the already-complete arm's drop_task_link_from_mail, or record an explicit amendment narrowing §5.2's rule to the two enumerated dispositions. Do not leave the absolute rule and the narrowed implementation both standing. fenix's ruling: give the two rejection paths (third-party close, stale counterparty) a deliver-plain fallback like the already-complete arm's drop_task_link_from_mail, per design section 5.2's ordering rule." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/batch.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix (ATM 01M2ABSS6Y9SF66MQ1R5JSRQPH, 2026-09-12T08:30:02Z): pushed by arch-ctm at review-2 1dcfcdf32 (fix(tasks): retain rejected close reports as plain mail). Recorded fixed-pending-correction: two corrections requested (dead duplicate template-admission method; rejected template report must still persist its decomposition). Final headSha will be the correction commit, not 1dcfcdf32. Gates on 1dcfcdf32 in flight. fenix (ATM 01M2AC0XJT9PJWSGDYE220SD7R, 2026-09-12T08:33:56Z): remap -- correction commit 6096429ee accepted on review; status fixed-pending-gate at 6096429ee, fenix's gate run in flight. Gate-green confirmed (ATM 01M2AC6DXZ4Q9FBGQQ14EG9MM7, 2026-09-12T08:36:56Z): 13-gate-green on fenix's host (cli_surface 2/2); CPR-010 closed at 6096429ee." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
